  "theorem_name": "AdaptiveValuationCriterionEquivalenceAndRunBlockClosure",
  "declared_proposition": "For positive integers D and B, D does not divide B if and only if there exists a prime q with v_q(D)>v_q(B). Consequently TICKET-197's all-k nondivisibility theorem for D_k=32^k-27^k and B_k=32^k+27^k-2*18^k already implies a word-dependent prime-power valuation witness for every binary run block. Conversely, demanding such a witness for every primitive binary density-band necklace is exactly equivalent to universal affine nondivisibility on that class; it is not a weaker bridge toward that periodic-cycle exclusion.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Unique factorization gives D|B exactly when v_q(D)<=v_q(B) for every prime q. Negating this statement proves the equivalence. TICKET-197 proved D_k does not divide B_k for every k>=1 by reducing divisibility to the impossible inequality D_k<=3^k-2^k. Applying the valuation equivalence yields the run-block witness. The exact audit records one such prime for k=1,...,20 and checks both valuations directly.",
